--------------------

VibeTracker is an independent, unofficial project. It is not affiliated with,
endorsed by, or supported by Anthropic, OpenAI, Google, Microsoft, Cursor,
Cline, opencode, or any other vendor whose software it observes.

It reads files those programs write to the local filesystem. Those file formats
are undocumented and belong to their authors, who may change them at any time
and are under no obligation to keep this tool working. Where a format is
described in this repository -- in `packages/core/dialects/` -- it is a record
of what was observed on a real machine at a stated version, not a specification
anyone has agreed to.

The names of those products are used only to say which program's files are
being read, which is the "reasonable and customary use in describing the origin
of the Work" that Section 6 of the License permits. No trademark rights are
claimed or granted.


WHAT THIS SOFTWARE DOES NOT DO
------------------------------

Stated here because these are guarantees, not features, and a fork that removes
them should have to do so deliberately:

  * It never writes to a project directory.
  * It never writes to, deletes from, or modifies an agent's state directory.
  * It never opens credential files.
  * It never captures process command lines.
  * It makes no network request of its own. The LLM digest is off by default
    and, when enabled, sends only what it shows you first.

See PRIVACY.md for the full account.


THIRD-PARTY CONTENT
-------------------

This distribution has no runtime dependencies. Nothing is vendored, bundled, or
statically linked into the published package.

Development dependencies (TypeScript, and the Node.js toolchain) are not
redistributed and carry their own licenses.

Desktop builds, where produced, bundle a Node.js runtime and the Tauri
framework; their licenses travel with those artifacts.
